{"ts": "2026-08-17T13:00:14Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 16, "kind": "message", "text": "Both the spec and design explicitly call out this feature as frontend-only \u2014 no changes to `backend/`, `store.py`, or `api.js`, since the deferred-delete approach never mutates the task's local state, so nothing needs reconstructing server-side.\n\nMy assigned scope is backend, and the spec's \"Affected areas\" section (`docs/spec.md:76-95`) confirms there is nothing in `backend/` for this ticket. I verified this rather than assuming \u2014 the existing `DELETE /api/tasks/{id}` route and its 404 behavior (`backend/app/main.py:69`) are reused unmodified.\n\n**Handoff:**\n\nNo backend changes are required for Taiga #13. The spec/design's core design decision is to implement the undo window entirely in `App.jsx` by deferring the `DELETE` API call for 5 seconds rather than firing it immediately \u2014 since the task is only hidden from view (not mutated or removed from state) during that window, undo is a pure frontend state operation. `backend/app/main.py`, `backend/app/store.py`, and `frontend/src/api.js` are all reused unmodified.\n\nI ran no commands and made no edits, since there is nothing in this scope to implement. The frontend-scope developer instance (working on `App.jsx`, `TaskList.jsx`, new `UndoToast.jsx`, `App.css`) owns the entire feature. No backend tests need updating either, since the existing `DELETE /api/tasks/{id}` route's behavior (including its 404-on-missing semantics, which AC6 relies on) is unchanged.", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "d035ae61-0ca8-4ddf-9442-515e660aa08b"}}
